/** @mainpage Qore avro Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section avrointro avro Module Introduction

    The \c avro module implements <a href="https://avro.apache.org">Apache Avro</a> for %Qore:
    schema parsing, the binary datum codec in both directions, object container files, and
    reader/writer schema resolution.

    Avro is schema-driven. The encoded bytes carry no field names, no tags and no type markers —
    just values packed in schema order — so nothing can be decoded without the schema, and the
    schema is itself a JSON document. The module therefore supports both framings that occur in
    practice:

    - a <b>bare datum</b>, which has no framing at all and is decoded against a schema supplied
      out of band, typically resolved at runtime by ID; this is what streaming APIs such as the
      <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/overview">Salesforce
      Pub/Sub API</a> deliver
    - an <b>object container file</b>, which is self-describing: the schema and codec are in the
      header, followed by blocks of records

    @section avrocapabilities Key Capabilities

    - full schema parsing with a named-type registry, so recursive and re-referenced types work
    - every Avro type: \c null, \c boolean, \c int, \c long, \c float, \c double, \c bytes,
      \c string, \c record, \c enum, \c array, \c map, \c union and \c fixed
    - every logical type: \c decimal (at arbitrary precision), \c uuid, \c date, \c time-millis,
      \c time-micros, \c timestamp-millis, \c timestamp-micros, \c local-timestamp-millis,
      \c local-timestamp-micros and \c duration
    - reader/writer schema resolution following the specification's reconciliation rules
    - object container files with the \c null and \c deflate codecs, over a file path, a
      \c binary value, or a %Qore @ref Qore::InputStream "InputStream" /
      @ref Qore::OutputStream "OutputStream"
    - Parsing Canonical Form and the CRC-64-AVRO fingerprint, for content-addressed schema caches
    - a companion <a href="../../AvroUtil/html/index.html#avroutilintro">AvroUtil</a> user
      module mapping Avro schemas to
      <a href="../../DataProvider/html/index.html#dataproviderintro">data provider</a> types

    @section avroclasses avro Module Classes

    |!Class|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Avro::AvroSchema "AvroSchema"|a parsed, immutable schema; parses schema JSON and \
        encodes and decodes bare data against it
    |@ref Qore::Avro::AvroFileReader "AvroFileReader"|reads an object container file; an \
        @ref Qore::AbstractIterator "AbstractIterator" over the objects it holds
    |@ref Qore::Avro::AvroFileWriter "AvroFileWriter"|writes an object container file

    @section avroquickstart At a Glance

    @code{.py}
%requires avro

AvroSchema schema('{"type": "record", "name": "Event", "fields": [
    {"name": "id", "type": "string"},
    {"name": "count", "type": "long"}
]}');

binary data = schema.encode({"id": "a", "count": 1});
hash<auto> event = schema.decode(data);
    @endcode

